0022: mesh read-back for the Direct3D 9 shadow tiles (real-time GI work package MC-3). Client exports RemixBridge_GiMeshFetch(lite, &ticket) and RemixBridge_GiMeshRead(ticket, pos, maxVertices, tri, maxTriangles, &vertices, &triangles): the GI worker resolves the LITE through the package index of patch 0020 (built first if no object batch has) and writes the model's caster mesh (shadow LOD, else LOD 0; model space, xyz floats a vertex, abc a triangle) into GiMeshSlot, a 256 KB mapping of its own ("GiMesh"), so the GI block keeps its layout. One fetch is in flight at a time: a second fetch answers D3DERR_WASSTILLDRAWING until the first is read. The read answers S_FALSE while pending, D3DERR_NOTFOUND for a LITE without a mesh, D3DERR_MOREDATA for a mesh over the slot or the caller's arrays. Counter word 21 of RemixBridge_GiReadCounters counts the answers. Test: test-gi-mesh.cmd (test_gi_mesh_device: the chair read back equal to the package reader's, an unknown LITE, a short array, 50 timed fetches).
Applies after 0021 (both append to Commands and the .def); uses the package index of 0020.
